Early Game
----------

1) Protection is critical. Getting your AC down in the early game is
really important. Shopping and/or wearing armor to get your AC down
along with buying as much protection as you can from the Minetown
priest is essential.

2) Pets are really your best friend. Feed them corpses while you pray
to relieve hunger. Let them gain experience and HP by having them take
out monsters. Dogs and cats really love tripe and will clear out a whole
shop if you feed it to them after they drop something they picked up in
the shop at your feet. You can acquire new doggies and kitties during the
game. Two or maybe even three can really help you. Search for magic whistles
in shops and in the Mines. It's a valuable tool to help track your pets 
and have them call to your aid.

3) Being able to heal will take you a long way towards your goal. Healing
Potions of all types, healing spellbooks, and rings of regen can help keep
you off the skids.

4) Travel light. Many nethackers have the tendency to want to carry
everything. Being burdened slows you down. I generally ditch spellbooks
in Minetown as they are heavy. Gaining strength to carry stuff is helpful.

5) Experience and levels are a dual edged sword. While you get HPs and
power points with each level, the monsters become tougher as you level up.

6) The holy grails of the early game are holy water and some method of
IDing stuff. The 4 sub $100 scrolls are all really helpful (enchant
armor, enchant weapon, ID, and remove curse). Use the store to get those
IDed. Hope that the Altar in Minetown (or some other alter in the main
dungeon) is co-alinged. If so then start sacrificing everything you can
on that altar to appease you god and hopefully get holy water which makes
almost every potion and spell in the game better. You'll also need it for
your unicorn horn.

My general strategy in the early game (up to Sokoban and Mines end) is to
level up the pets, lower the AC (I usually compomise at naked AC 1) and
gather tools for the next phase.

Mid Game
--------
This usually starts with finishing up Sokoban or Mines end. With my AC
down between -10 to -15 and pets leveled up to max level and HP, I finally
start to level up myself by whacking on monsters. Towards the end of the
mines the polymorph traps start to show up. When you find one, go ahead 
and poly your pets up to something that can grow even more powerful.
I really loved my mind flayer/orange dragon pair. Just be careful because
ultra high level pets will kill and eat shopkeeper and priests.

Next on the list are five properties of note:

1) Reflection
2) Magic Resistance
3) Weight reduction
4) Good weapon
5) Useful spells

Usually this will involve a wish or two, so smoky potions, magic lamps,
and thrones are helpful. Note that they work best when blessed, so back
to the holy water. I generally will dilute useless potions and then
bless them. Same with a luckstone. Get it in mines end and bless it.

Late Game
--------
This is from the quest until dealing with Rodney. Instant death and
getting crowned by continual praying are the big deals here. You want
to get resistance to everything including disintegration. Also you want
to fix all your equipment so that it won't rust or burn. blessed bags
of holding are essential for carrying stuff. You'll get a guaranteed
wand of wishing in the castle, so you can pick and choose whatever
gaps you have.

